A||||6||mrfixit58||Sunroof Install||||5||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||04-28-2000||10:48 AM||||I'm looking at an 88 GT that is pretty cherry. It has just about everything I want in a GT except a sunroof. I have axcess to a wreaked GT with a suroof and it's even the right color. Now the obvious question...<P>How hard is it to change a roof panel? Do I have to pull the windshield? It looks like I may have to pull the front fenders as well. Is this difficult? Is there anything else I need to look out for to do this swap?<P>Thanks in advance,<BR>Roy<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||TOM||04-28-2000||10:57 AM||||Front fenders just need to have a couple of bolts removed and flexed a little outward when ready to remove and install the panel. Windshield does NOT need to be removed. I did one and it is pretty straight forward. If you need more info just let me know.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||04-28-2000||11:04 AM||||Thanks Tom,<P>If the deal is made then I'll DEFINATLY get back to you.<P>Roy||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||04-28-2000||02:31 PM||||We did the same swap on an 86. The only 2 things that are difficult is first there is a tar like substance that holds the front of the roof down. To aid in breaking the seal we used a 30" piece of metal as a blade and inched it along the edge. This takes the most time to do but go slow so you don't damage the windshield (or roof if your saving the old). One small chip on the windshield can end up as a large crack over time. The only other thing to be VERY careful is the corners where the roof meets the side struts that run next to the windshield. This is the most fragile part of the roof and can crack easily. It is easier with 2 people to remove and install the new roof. Just go slow and careful. It took us about 3 hours to remove both roofs and install the one with the sunroof. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||lennyb4||04-28-2000||02:39 PM||||Man i love these cars..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I want to put a sun roof in and thought id have to cut the top (good thing i didnt start yesterday like i wanted to), but if its that easy then i'll just do the whole roof thing..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||04-28-2000||03:30 PM||||Heating the panel (hair dryer) to soften the adheasive helps too. Don't forget to get the head liner and the little plastic visor ||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||04-29-2000||03:03 PM||||There is a tool for removing windshields that should work for this as well.<P>The tool has one handle that is tipped with an L shaped blade. The other is a T handle attached to the first just above the blade.<P>You use the main handle to insert and guide the blade. you use the T handle to pull the blade allong what you are cutting.<P>A good one of these is a little hard to find but makes this type thing relatively easy.||||reg||1
